What qualities should a good leaner have?
There are quite a few qualities. Firstly, a learner must have the ability to manage time effectively. After getting a job or having a family, many people have less time to focus solely on acquiring knowledge. Thus, the ability to plan and utilize fragmented time for learning becomes extremely important. Secondly, a learner should be diligent and persistent. In fact, learning any skill is the accumulation of effective learning time. Take the 10,000-time rule for example. Even if one doesn't reach 10,000 hours, studying for 20 minutes every day can lead to significant gains in a year.

Why do people prefer to study alone?
Well, the cause is largely due to personal inclination. For instance, they enjoy the flexibility that allows them to set their own pace and schedule. Say, if they are night owls and feel more energetic in the evening, they can choose to study then. Also, they tend to learn more effectively and don't need to worry about coordinating with other' schedules. Moreover studying alone offers a more concentrated environment with significantly fewer distractions. It enables them to fully immerse themselves in the learning process without any interruptions.

